# Work directly on main — hard requirement

- Work only on the existing `main` branch.
- Do not create, switch to, or push another branch.
- Do not create a pull request.
- Do not use a temporary stabilization branch.
- Do not use a separate Git worktree attached to another branch.
- Before editing, verify that the current branch is `main`.
- Fetch `origin/main` before beginning.
- Safely integrate the latest compatible `origin/main` state.
- Commit every coherent logical step directly on `main`.
- Push completed commits directly to `origin/main`.
- Push regularly so completed logical steps are not left only in the local repository.
- Never force-push.
- Never rewrite published history.
- Never amend a commit that has already been pushed unless explicitly authorized.
- If a push is rejected because `origin/main` advanced:
  - fetch the latest remote state;
  - integrate compatible remote changes safely;
  - preserve current local and other-agent work;
  - rerun all affected tests;
  - push normally.
- If repository protection prevents direct pushes to `main`, stop and report **BLOCKED**.
- Do not create a branch or pull request as a workaround.
- The task is incomplete until the final verified code, tests, fixtures, workflows, and documentation are pushed to `origin/main`.
<!-- MEW-MAIN-DIRECT_END -->
